@baseUrl = http://localhost:5080

### Health check (database connectivity)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Register a new member (role is always Member)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "New",
  "lastName": "Member",
  "email": "new.member@fitforge.test",
  "password": "Str0ng!Pass",
  "confirmPassword": "Str0ng!Pass",
  "phoneNumber": "+91 98765 43210"
}

### Login (copy accessToken from the response into @token below)
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "rahul.member@fitforge.test",
  "password": "<demo password from user secrets>"
}

### Current user
@token = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Refresh (uses the HttpOnly cookie set by login; the header is required)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/refresh
X-FitForge-Client: web

### Logout
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout
X-FitForge-Client: web

### Forgot password (in development the reset link is written to the API console)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "rahul.member@fitforge.test" }
